# Backend (FastAPI) – Fleet Tracking Prototype

This backend ingests telemetry (Millitrack polling or simulation), publishes normalized messages to Redis channel `telemetry`, optionally stores raw telemetry in Postgres, and broadcasts updates via Socket.IO (`/socket.io`) and a plain WebSocket (`/ws`).

## Quick start (Docker Compose dev)

### Unix
```sh
cd backend
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env (set MILLITRACK_TOKEN if you have one)
docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up --build
```

### PowerShell
```powershell
Set-Location backend
Copy-Item .env.example .env -Force
# Edit .env (set MILLITRACK_TOKEN if you have one)
docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up --build
```

Backend will be on: http://localhost:8000
- Health: http://localhost:8000/health
- Metrics: http://localhost:8000/metrics
- Socket.IO: http://localhost:8000/socket.io
- WebSocket: ws://localhost:8000/ws

## Run locally (no Docker)

### Unix
```sh
cd backend
python3 -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
export REDIS_ENABLED=false
export LOG_LEVEL=info
export POLL_INTERVAL=10
export MILLITRACK_TOKEN=
export DATABASE_URL=
export SIMULATE_ON_STARTUP=true
uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload
```

### PowerShell
```powershell
Set-Location backend
py -3 -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -r requirements.txt
$env:REDIS_ENABLED='false'
$env:LOG_LEVEL='info'
$env:POLL_INTERVAL='10'
$env:MILLITRACK_TOKEN=''
$env:DATABASE_URL=''
$env:SIMULATE_ON_STARTUP='true'
uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload
```

## Migration (optional Postgres)

Creates table `telemetry_raw`.

### Unix
```sh
cd backend
python -m app.models
```

### PowerShell
```powershell
Set-Location backend
python -m app.models
```

If `DATABASE_URL` is not set, migration logs a warning and exits.

## Simulation mode (publishes fake telemetry to Redis)

### Unix
```sh
cd backend
python -m app.simulate
```

### PowerShell
```powershell
Set-Location backend
python -m app.simulate
```

## Alerts worker

Subscribes to `telemetry` and publishes alerts to Redis channel `alerts` when fuel drops by more than `ALERT_FUEL_DROP` within `ALERT_WINDOW_SECONDS`.

### Unix
```sh
cd backend
python -m app.alerts_worker
```

### PowerShell
```powershell
Set-Location backend
python -m app.alerts_worker
```

## Tests

